# Title: Potential Persistence Attempt Via Run Keys Using Reg.EXE
# ID: de587dce-915e-4218-aac4-835ca6af6f70
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2021-06-28
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.t1547.001
# Description: Detects suspicious command line reg.exe tool adding key to RUN key in Registry
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(process.executable:*\\reg.exe AND (process.command_line:*reg* AND process.command_line:* add *) AND (process.command_line:*Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run* OR process.command_line:*\\Software\\WOW6432Node\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run* OR process.command_line:*\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\Run*))
